Call a capability from your shell, host a peer, inspect a live session in the
REPL, or expose CapTP tools over MCP (Model Context Protocol, which AI
assistants use to call tools), with the library's [Host]($link.page('modules')).
The [CLI guide](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/docs/cli.md)
is the complete reference.

Install the [CLI + Rooms product](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/apps/rooms/host.md#install)
in one command. It verifies the download against the release checksums before
running the product's installer:

```sh
curl -fsSL https://glowcap.org/install.sh | sh
```

[GitHub Releases](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/releases) has the
same `glowcap-vVERSION-ARCH-OS.tar.gz` archives to install by hand, and the
`glowcap-c-` download contains the C SDK for building applications.

```sh
glowcap help
```

# Join a room over iroh

Rooms needs the [complete installation](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/apps/rooms/host.md),
including its services and browser assets. This command starts your workspace
from the shell in the directory you name, and its peers talk over
[iroh]($link.page('transports/iroh')), an encrypted QUIC transport:

```sh
glowcap apps rooms session start --dir=./rooms-session
```

# A local round-trip

`ocapn listen` binds loopback `tcp`, the testing transport: a cleartext
`host:port` with no identity proof. The CLI's demo greeter answers the verb
`greet` with `Hello, <arg>`.

Each terminal sets its own `GLOWCAP_STATE` directory, so it acts as its own
peer, and `init` creates the identity keys that peer signs its sessions with.
Run terminal A first, then paste its printed locator (the peer's dialable
`ocapn://` address) into `LOC` in terminal B. `--publish` serves one partner
and then exits, and `Ctrl+C` or `SIGTERM` stops a waiting or serving `listen`
cleanly with exit 0.

```sh
# terminal A
export GLOWCAP_STATE=/tmp/glowcap-a
glowcap --json init
glowcap --json ocapn listen --publish greeter
# {"ok":true,"locator":"ocapn://127.0.0.1%3A46659.tcp"}   (%3A is the : of host:port, URI-encoded)

# terminal B
export GLOWCAP_STATE=/tmp/glowcap-b
glowcap --json init
LOC='ocapn://127.0.0.1%3A46659.tcp'   # paste A's locator
glowcap --json ocapn call "$LOC" greeter greet world
#                         name──┘       │     └─ arg
#                         verb──────────┘
# {"ok":true,"value":"Hello, world"}
```

# REPL, MCP, and completion

`glowcap repl` is an interactive CapTP session. Start it empty and dial from
inside, or pass a locator to dial first. In a terminal it shows the session's
exports, imports, and answers beside the prompt as you type. Type `guide` for
a staged walkthrough. The
[CLI guide](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/blob/main/docs/cli.md) has
recipes for the REPL and for `probe`, which needs a live listener to dial.

```sh
glowcap mcp --tools default                # CapTP tools for an editor assistant (MCP)
eval "$(glowcap completion bash)"          # tab completion
```

For the library API behind these commands, continue to [Start
building]($link.page('start')). The [demo apps]($link.page('examples')) use the
same operations in a chat room, a task board, and a tool service.
